## 2. Low Level Design (LLD) - Microservice Internal Architecture

This diagram shows the internal structure of a typical microservice in this project (e.g., Application Service). It follows a standard layered architecture using Spring Boot.

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph Typical Microservice Architecture
        direction TB
        C[Controller Layer<br/>Handles HTTP & Routing]
        S[Service Layer<br/>Business & Transaction Logic]
        R[Repository Layer<br/>Spring Data JPA]
        E[(Database)]
        
        M[Mapper / DTOs<br/>Data Transformation]
    end
    
    ClientRequest[HTTP Request] --> C
    C -->|Uses| M
    C -->|Invokes| S
    S -->|Invokes| R
    R -->|SQL Queries| E
    
    E -.->|Entity Data| R
    R -.->|Entity Data| S
    S -.->|DTO| C
    C -.->|HTTP Response| ClientResponse[HTTP Response]
```

---

## 3. Flow Diagram - Loan Application Submission & Document Upload

This sequence diagram illustrates the workflow of a user submitting a loan application and subsequently uploading supporting documents.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as React Frontend
    participant Gateway as API Gateway
    participant Auth as Auth Service
    participant App as Application Service
    participant Doc as Document Service
    participant DB as MySQL DB
    participant Dropbox as Dropbox API

    Note over Client,Gateway: Loan Application Creation
    Client->>Gateway: POST /api/applications (Form Data, JWT)
    Gateway->>Auth: Validate JWT Token
    Auth-->>Gateway: Token Valid (User ID extracted)
    Gateway->>App: Forward Request
    App->>DB: Save Application (Status: PENDING)
    DB-->>App: Saved Application Entity
    App-->>Gateway: 201 Created (Application ID)
    Gateway-->>Client: Application Created Success

    Note over Client,Gateway: Document Upload
    Client->>Gateway: POST /api/documents (App ID, File, JWT)
    Gateway->>Auth: Validate JWT Token
    Auth-->>Gateway: Token Valid
    Gateway->>Doc: Forward Request (Multipart File)
    Doc->>Dropbox: Upload File via DbxClientV2
    Dropbox-->>Doc: File Metadata & Shareable Link
    Doc->>DB: Save Document Record (URL, App ID)
    DB-->>Doc: Saved Document Entity
    Doc-->>Gateway: 201 Created (Document Info)
    Gateway-->>Client: Document Upload Success
```

---

## 4. Admin Dashboard Data Aggregation Flow

This diagram shows how the Admin service fetches data from various services to present a unified dashboard.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant AdminApp as Admin React Frontend
    participant Gateway as API Gateway
    participant AdminSvc as Admin Service
    participant AppSvc as Application Service
    participant AuthSvc as Auth Service

    AdminApp->>Gateway: GET /api/admin/dashboard (Admin JWT)
    Gateway->>AdminSvc: Forward Request
    
    par Parallel Data Fetching
        AdminSvc->>AppSvc: GET /api/applications/stats
        AppSvc-->>AdminSvc: Return Application Statistics
    and
        AdminSvc->>AuthSvc: GET /api/users/stats
        AuthSvc-->>AdminSvc: Return User Statistics
    end
    
    AdminSvc->>AdminSvc: Aggregate Stats (Total Users, Loans, etc.)
    AdminSvc-->>Gateway: Combined Dashboard DTO
    Gateway-->>AdminApp: 200 OK Dashboard Data
```
